.\" halite-node(8)
.\"
.\" mdoc rather than man(7): this project's fleet is mostly FreeBSD,
.\" mdoc is what a FreeBSD port expects, and groff reads it on Linux.
.\" Section 8 because every one of these commands administers a machine
.\" and most of them need root.
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt HALITE-NODE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm halite-node
.Nd managed endpoint agent and local executor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Op Fl -flag Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the agent that runs on a managed machine.
It executes module functions, compiles and applies state trees, and holds
a stream open to a hub that gives it work.
.Pp
It has two modes.
With
.Fl -local
it works entirely from its own configuration and its own file roots and
needs no hub, which is what Salt calls masterless.
.Sq lexicon:allow
Without it, the tree, the pillar and the jobs come from the hub named in
the configuration.
.Pp
Nothing but the commands marked below changes anything on the machine.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "state apply"
.It Cm call Ar module.function Op Ar args ...
Run one execution module function and print what it returned.
Positional arguments are given in order; keyword arguments are given as
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value .
.It Cm state Ar subcommand Op Ar args ...
Compile or apply a state tree.
.Cm state apply
applies the highstate,
.Cm state apply Ar sls
applies one file, and
.Cm state show
compiles without applying.
With
.Fl -test
nothing is changed and the result is what would have changed.
.It Cm grains Oo Cm items | item | get | ls Oc Op Ar key
Read this node's grains.
.Cm get
takes one key and answers with its value;
.Cm item
takes any number and answers with a mapping.
.It Cm pillar Oo Cm items | item | get Oc Op Ar key
Read this node's pillar, compiled by the hub or from local roots.
.It Cm lint Ar path
Render and parse a file without executing anything in it.
Templates are rendered, so a
.Sy #!yaml|gpg
file is decrypted.
.It Cm doctor
Run the diagnostics of the specification's section 26.4 and print a
pass, warning, failure or skip for each, with a line saying what to do
about anything that is not a pass.
Changes nothing.
Exits non-zero only on a failure, so a warning does not fail a cron job
or a state's
.Sy onlyif .
.It Cm enroll
Ask a hub for a certificate.
The first request is pending until an operator accepts it; the second
collects the certificate.
.It Cm renew
Replace this node's certificate before it expires.
.It Cm connect
Hold the stream to the hub open and run what it sends.
.Cm serve
is an alias.
This is what the service unit runs.
.It Cm event send Ar tag Op Ar json
Put an event on the hub's bus.
.It Cm version
Print the build identity: version, commit, and the Go toolchain.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--pillar-root dir"
.It Fl -help
Describe the program without running the command.
.It Fl -local
Work from local roots rather than through a hub.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Configuration file.
Defaults to
.Pa node.yaml
under the configuration root.
.It Fl -root Ar dir
Configuration root.
.It Fl -file-root Ar dir
A state root, repeatable.
Implies
.Fl -local .
.It Fl -pillar-root Ar dir
A pillar root, repeatable.
Implies
.Fl -local .
.It Fl -env Ar name
Environment, default
.Sy base .
.It Fl -pillarenv Ar name
Pillar environment, defaulting to
.Fl -env .
.It Fl -id Ar node-id
Override the node identity.
.It Fl -out Ar format
.Sy nested
(default),
.Sy json ,
.Sy yaml ,
.Sy txt ,
or
.Sy quiet .
.It Fl -test
Run every state in test mode, changing nothing.
.It Fl -permissive
Allow undefined template names, as Salt does.
.Sq lexicon:allow
.El
.Pp
.Cm enroll
and
.Cm connect
take further options; see
.Nm
.Fl -help .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/halite/node.yaml" -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/halite/node.yaml
Configuration on the BSDs.
.It Pa /etc/halite/node.yaml
Configuration elsewhere.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/halite/pki
Key material: this node's certificate and key, and the hub's CA.
.It Pa /var/db/halite
Durable state on the BSDs;
.Pa /var/lib/halite
elsewhere.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
A state run that applied cleanly exits 0.
A run with a failed state exits non-zero.
.Cm doctor
exits non-zero only when a check fails, not when one warns.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Apply the highstate from local roots, changing nothing:
.Pp
.Dl halite-node state apply --local --test
.Pp
Ask what is wrong with this machine:
.Pp
.Dl halite-node doctor
.Pp
Read one grain:
.Pp
.Dl halite-node grains get os --local
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halite-hub 8 ,
.Xr halite-api 8
.Pp
The command reference, the operations guide and the configuration
reference ship in
.Pa docs/
in the source tree.
